menu "SWD Engine Configuration"

config DEBUG_SWDIO_GPIO
    int "SWDIO GPIO number"
    default 5
    range 0 48
    help
        GPIO connected to the target SWDIO pin (core board header J1).

config DEBUG_SWCLK_GPIO
    int "SWCLK GPIO number"
    default 4
    range 0 48
    help
        GPIO connected to the target SWCLK pin (core board header J1).

config DEBUG_NRESET_GPIO
    int "nRESET GPIO number (-1 = not connected)"
    default 6
    range -1 48
    help
        GPIO connected to the target nRESET pin. Set to -1 if not wired.
        Driven open-drain (never pushed high), internal pull-up enabled.

config DEBUG_SWD_DEFAULT_CLOCK_HZ
    int "Default SWD clock (Hz)"
    default 100000
    help
        Stage-1 bring-up clock. Fix stability at 100 kHz first (connect under
        reset, DPIDR, CTRLSTAT, MEM-AP, DHCSR), then raise step by step
        (400k / 1M / 2M / 5M). Never sacrifice 100k/400k stability for speed.

config DEBUG_SWD_TRACE
    bool "Enable SWD connect/diagnostic trace logs"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, logs the SWD clock, JTAG->SWD switch, DPIDR, CTRLSTAT,
        AP IDR and per-stage connect results. Never affects the bit-level
        hot path (swd_transfer stays IRAM + log-free).

config DEBUG_SWD_MAX_CLOCK_HZ
    int "Maximum SWD clock (Hz)"
    default 8000000
    range 100000 20000000
    help
        Soft cap applied by DAP_SWJ_Clock. Bit-banged SWD on ESP32-S3 has
        been verified up to this frequency; raise only after testing.

endmenu
